- Final 18–20-ft. well 15–45 PBI;
- Proposed 688-ft. well.

core.figure_description:
----
━━━ FORMAT 4: CROSS-SECTION / РАЗРЕЗ ━━━
(a) Southwest–Northeast correlation section.

Vertical scale: depth; numerical labels 8500, 8600, 8700 at left and 8400, 8500, 8600 at right. Depth increases downward. Units are not printed.

Wells, from southwest to northeast:
1. 11-28
2. 11-30
3. 11-23

Lithologic/depositional units shown by colour:
- yellow-orange — Fluvial/Crevasse Splay;
- bright yellow — Floodplain;
- yellow — Distributary Channel;
- orange — Distributary Mouth Bar;
- pale beige — Bay;
- light yellow — Shelf, Prodelta, & Delta Front.

Fluid legend:
- black — Gas;
- white — Oil.

The section contains several laterally continuous black gas intervals, with white oil intervals and coloured depositional bodies between them. A vertical black well trajectory is shown at well 11-30, curving toward the southwest at approximately depth 8650–8680. At well 11-23, a vertical log-like curve is displayed beside the well.

